<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Daniel Noboa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1987">1987</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Daniel Noboa is an Ecuadorian businessman and politician, the son of the banana <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a> Álvaro Noboa. He won the early election of 2023 that followed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guillermo-lasso">Guillermo Lasso</a>'s dissolution of the National Assembly, becoming one of the youngest presidents in Ecuador's history. In January 2024 he declared an internal armed conflict against criminal gangs, and he was re-elected in April 2025.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/daniel-noboa.jpg" alt="Daniel Noboa" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juan Montenegro/Presidencia de la República · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Noboa_en_24_mayo_de_2026.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
